{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implementation will be in Go, extending an existing fabric channel configuration library (e.g., fabric-config or similar configtx helper package) since Hyperledger Fabric is Go-based.",
    "Each new helper function will follow the existing builder/update pattern in the package, returning a value or error so the caller can chain further configuration updates and produce a ConfigUpdate envelope.",
    "The ConfigUpdate envelope computation is delegated to existing helper utilities (e.g., a ComputeConfigUpdate function); new functions only mutate the in-memory Config structure.",
    "For capabilities (U5), the toggle approach (EnableV20_X / DisableV20_X) is preferred over arbitrary string setters, because the spec says 'Consider whether we should allow setting unsupported capabilities... or if we should just have toggles'. This avoids typos and unsupported values.",
    "For U4, three separate getter functions (one per capability type: orderer, application, channel) are provided rather than a single multi-purpose function, for clarity and idiomatic Go usage.",
    "U3 (getOrgPolicies) and U6 (getApplicationConfig) are read-only helpers that return strongly-typed config.Application / []config.Policy structures so callers do not need to manually traverse the protos.",
    "U7 ACL helpers modify a single Application group's ACLs in place; both Add and Remove variants are provided for symmetry with existing add/remove patterns in the package.",
    "U8 refactoring keeps existing assertion behavior and code coverage, but reorganizes the monolithic example test into five focused, named example tests that each demonstrate one slice of functionality.",
    "Unit tests and the example test described in the spec are treated as part of each activity's deliverable, not a separate phase.",
    "No new dependencies are introduced; all work is contained in the existing config package."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "One experienced Go developer who already knows the Hyperledger Fabric config package performs all work, including design, implementation, testing, and example updates.",
    "1 workday = 8 productive hours (no overhead subtracted for meetings, etc., because the task is the developer's total software development effort).",
    "The starting code base already contains analogous functions (e.g., addOrdererOrg, removeApplicationOrg, anchor peer helpers), so the new functions can reuse shared internal helpers for navigating OrdererGroups/ApplicationGroups.",
    "The example test referenced in the acceptance criteria is an integration/example test that lives alongside the package (e.g., in an examples/ directory) and exercises the new functions end-to-end on a realistic Config block.",
    "Code review, CI, and merging are not counted as part of development effort; only authoring, local testing, and example demonstration are.",
    "No documentation beyond standard Go doc comments and the example test is required (e.g., no separate markdown guide).",
    "All protobuf/generated structures referenced (config.Application, config.Capabilities, config.Policy) already exist in the codebase and do not need to be created or modified."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A0",
      "activity_name": "Codebase exploration and shared helper design",
      "activity_description": "Review existing config package functions, identify shared internal helpers to reuse for endpoint/ACL/capability operations, and confirm the ConfigUpdate computation path used by the new functions."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Add orderer endpoint helper",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that takes an existing Config and adds an orderer endpoint to a given orderer org's config group, computes the ConfigUpdate, and extend the example test to demonstrate adding an orderer endpoint."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Remove orderer endpoint helper",
      "activity_description": "Implement the symmetric remove function for an orderer endpoint from an orderer org's config group and add a corresponding example."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Get organization policies helper",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that retrieves the existing policies for a given organization regardless of whether it is an application, orderer, or consortium org, returning a typed policy collection, and update the example test."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Get capabilities helpers",
      "activity_description": "Implement three getter functions (orderer, application, channel capabilities) that each return a config.Capabilities value from a Config block/transaction."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Add/remove (enable/disable) capabilities",
      "activity_description": "Implement Enable/Disable toggle functions for application, orderer, and channel capabilities, allow further ConfigUpdate processing on the returned config, and extend the example test to demonstrate enabling/disabling capabilities."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Get application configuration helper",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that returns the existing application configuration as a config.Application value without manual proto traversal."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Add/remove application group ACLs",
      "activity_description": "Implement helpers to add and remove ACLs on an application group's configuration, allow further ConfigUpdate processing, and update the example test to demonstrate ACL changes."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Refactor example tests into focused cases",
      "activity_description": "Split the existing monolithic end-to-end example test into separate, smaller example tests covering: (a) orderer configuration incl. orderer policies, (b) application values incl. application policies, (c) organization management (add/remove orgs, anchor peers, orderer endpoints), (d) MSP modifications, (e) capabilities. Each example must independently compile and pass."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Integration testing, debugging, and cleanup",
      "activity_description": "Run the full example test suite and unit tests, fix any issues found across the new helpers and refactored examples, and perform final code cleanup (consistent naming, error wrapping, Go doc comments)."
    }
  ],
  "most_likely_effort": {
    "A0": 0.5,
    "A1": 1.5,
    "A2": 1.0,
    "A3": 1.5,
    "A4": 1.0,
    "A5": 2.0,
    "A6": 1.0,
    "A7": 1.5,
    "A8": 2.0,
    "A9": 1.5
  },
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 13.5
  }
}
```

